WEBVTT

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.160
You little piccaninny, you're going to kill yourself flying like that.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.200
Yes, you are.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.520
- But you as deep, Pops.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.380
- I'm sorry, I didn't hear you speak.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.230
- Didn't say nothing.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.520
- Didn't you?

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.960
- Mr. David Burke.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.370
- 607, sir.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.120
Four, mister?

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.120
Six.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.970
You hear that wind?

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.960
Man, I'm gonna get myself grounded out of the Air Force.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.350
That's what I'm gonna do.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:47.200
Ain't gonna fly this kind of crate anymore.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.880
Can you blame me?

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:30.000
Right on time, Slater, right on time.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.690
Right there, Yuley.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:37.170
Come in, come in.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:42.160
Here, let me help you off with your things.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.460
You're doing such a big old dog in New York.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:46.740
I never had a wife.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.880
Right on the button.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.710
That's what I'm looking for, Slater.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.270
Someone serious with a head for business.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.000
All right here, come on, over here.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.350
Here, hop.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.170
Whiskey?

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.290
I don't mind.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.290
Straighter with water.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:00.000
With water.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.350
- I got ice, you want ice? - No, just water.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.540
Make yourself comfortable, Slater, we gotta talk.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.300
Like a view?

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.400
You gotta hold a heap of it.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.900
I used to be able to afford a little space inside, too.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:23.300
But, we call this dump home, don't we, old boy?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.190
Not bad.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.160
Well, here's to our mutual benefit.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.620
May it be considerable.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.540
I guess you know all you had to know about me, Slater.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:35.700
I know something.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.110
All right, you tell me what you know. Go on.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.210
You said you wanted to talk to me.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.980
Since we knew a few people in common, I naturally wanted to come and find out.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:47.720
I mean the dirt.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.900
I know you were on the police force.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:53.760
You had a session with the state crime committee, and you got a year for contempt.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.390
Because I wouldn't talk.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.330
I was on the force 30 years.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.000
I had my own squad, and I knew everybody.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:11.440
everybody was my friend until they needed a patsy I know about you were two

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:16.610
stretches one for assault with a deadly weapon one for manslaughter every time

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:26.460
you get a decent job get off so big about you Burke come you make so much

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.000
noise you've been sniffing around trying to find a hole in the fence just

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.870
Just like everybody else.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:36.290
What makes you so big you can call me up to this dump and shoot off your mouth?

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.730
I got an idea, that's why, Slater.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:43.130
How would you like to pick up $50,000 all in small bills just for yourself?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:54.340
How would you?

00:06:54.340 --> 00:07:00.000
Johnny?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:15.360
no when sure that's fine what would i have to do just walk into a bank and take it

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:26.230
got me wrong burke i never stole nothing in my life except maybe a watermelon when

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:30.000
i was a boy on the farm i'd want a big joe with more decorations than dylan's

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.040
I want a safe thing, a man who needs some money to set himself up.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:40.190
I want a man with guts, I want a serious guy in trouble, and that's you, that's me, that's

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:41.230
the both of us.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.310
This is a one-time job, one roll of the dice and then we're through forever.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.890
What do you say?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.990
Who'd like to make themselves a fortune?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.790
Now, everybody stays on the car, right?

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:40.010
- Do you? - Yeah.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:43.280
